  "developmentFailuresAndLessons": [
    "Initial raw-socket regression treated HTTP chunk framing as JSON. Changed the client to the real Node HTTP parser while retaining the partial-body timing and real WebSocket replacement.",
    "The execFile mock does not preserve its special promisify result metadata. The shared creation-time helper now uses an explicitly typed callback Promise; all consumers were rerun.",
    "The extra creation-time probes changed the last execFile mock call. Assert the signal call before performing later identity reads rather than inferring its meaning from an unrelated final call.",
    "Official CLI prerequisites must use the independently installed package under reference/runtime; a nested preparation fixture or omitted environment value is not accepted as verification."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No actual macOS kqueue host was available. The portable waitid branch was exercised with real Linux processes; this is not macOS acceptance.",
    "Portable POSIX scope remains the original process group; escaped setsid descendants require the Linux subreaper path and are not claimed for portable hosts.",
    "The identity regression models a predecessor birth identity at a currently live PID; it does not claim to have forced real kernel PID reuse.",
    "Controlled loopback providers and local MCP fixtures establish integration behavior, not commercial inference or external OAuth service availability."
  ],
